            <ArticleTitle>Idiopathic myoglobinuria in the early puerperium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>564-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myoglobinuria is rare in association with pregnancy. We report a case of idiopathic myoglobinuria in the early puerperium in a patient who had a spontaneous vaginal delivery. Acute muscular pain and port wine staining of the urine should alert the clinician.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
